{
  "dom_id": "step-q85305",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the region $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)\\le 1,\\,2{e}^{x}\\le y\\le 5{e}^{x}\\}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=\\frac{y}{{e}^{x}}$ and $v=x-2y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane.",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)\\le 1,\\,2{e}^{x}\\le y\\le 5{e}^{x}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,{e}^{0}\\le {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)}\\le {e}^{1},\\,\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{{e}^{x}}\\le \\frac{y}{{e}^{x}}\\le \\frac{5{e}^{x}}{{e}^{x}}\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le x-2y\\le e,\\,2\\le \\frac{y}{{e}^{x}}\\le 5\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le v\\le e,\\,2\\le u\\le 5\\} \\\\  & =\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 5,\\,1\\le v\\le e\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
